<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92514" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῑπ-ή</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥίπτω</span>) poet. Noun, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>swing</i> or <i>force with which anything is
			thrown</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσση δ᾽ αἰγανέης ῥιπὴ . .
				τέτυκται</span> as far as is the <i>flight</i> of a
			javelin, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				16.589
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λᾶος ὑπὸ ῥιπῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					12.462
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.192
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέτριναι ῥ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				1123
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βελέων ῥ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				1.68
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ ῥιπῆς . . Βορέαο</span>
			<i>the sweep</i> or <i>rush</i> of the N. wind, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				15.171
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				19.358
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				B.
				5.46
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυμάτων ῥιπαὶ ἀνέμων τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					4.195
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Parth.</u>
				2.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				88.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥ. ἀνέμων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>P.</u>
					9.48
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				137
			</span></i> (lyr., here metaph. of <i>gusts</i> of passion, cf. <i><span class="en">
				930
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥ. Διόθεν τεύχουσα φόβον</span>
			<i>storm</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				1089
			</span></i> (anap.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.1016
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥ. πυρός</span>
			<i>rush</i> of fire, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				21.12
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					8.355
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀθανάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					681
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				849
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεραυνῶν, χαλάζης</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				3.21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				14.77
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ ῥιπῇς
			Ἀφροδίτης</span>, of love, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				4.141
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νυχιᾶν </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐννυχιᾶν</span> Lachm.) <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ ῥιπᾶν</span> from the night <i>storms</i>, i.e.
			from the <u>North</u>, the land of darkness and storms,
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1248
			</span></i> (lyr., but Sch. understands <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥιπᾶν</span>, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥῖπαι</span>
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτερύγων ῥιπαί</span>
			<i>flapping</i> of wings, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				126
			</span></i> (anap.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				594.4
			</span></i>; <i>buzz</i> of a gnat's wing, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				893
			</span></i>; of the lyre's <i>quivering notes</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				1.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>quivering, twinkling light</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥιπαὶ ἄστρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					106
				</span></i>
			 (anap.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> of any
				<i>rapid movement</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥ. ποδῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IT</u>
					885
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥ. ὠκυάλῳ</span>, of a
			dolphin, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				2.535
			</span></i>; of a bird's wing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδὲ τινάσσει ῥιπήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.935
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ῥ. ὀφθαλμοῦ</span> the
				<i>twinkling</i> of an eye, <u>1 Ep.Cor.</u>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				15.52
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>a strong smell</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥ. οἴνου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					166
				</span></i>
			.</div>
